    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Design your onboarding system with progressive disclosure. New engineers should encounter information in layers: essential context on day one, deeper technical details in week two, nuanced trade-offs and historical decisions in month two. Structure your wiki accordingly. The top-level onboarding page should link to role-specific tracks (backend, frontend, SRE, mobile), and each track should be organized chronologically with clear \"Week 1,\" \"Week 2-4,\" \"Month 2-3\" sections. Within each period, distinguish between required material (must read/do) and optional material (useful but not blocking). This structure reduces overwhelm and helps engineers prioritize."
